<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy | Home AI Telegram Bot" %>

<article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-6 text-slate-800">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold">Privacy Policy</h1>

  <p>Last updated: November 20, 2026</p>

  <section class="space-y-2">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Google Calendar data</h2>
    <p>
      Home AI Telegram Bot accesses Google Calendar data only after an authorised
      household member connects a Google account. It uses that access to read
      calendar events and to create, update, or delete events that the household
      explicitly requests through the bot.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-2">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Storage and sharing</h2>
    <p>
      We store the OAuth tokens needed to keep the Calendar connection active and
      the calendar-event details required to provide the service. We do not sell,
      rent, or share Google Calendar data with third parties.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-2">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Revoking access</h2>
    <p>
      You can revoke the app's Google Calendar access at any time from your Google
      Account's third-party access settings. After access is revoked, the bot can no
      longer read or change your Google Calendar until you connect it again.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-2">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions, contact the household administrator through the
      Telegram bot.
    </p>
  </section>
</article>
